{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/gu5ffb","slide":2,"text":"The central idea is simple. Local evidence must retain design, uncertainty, and disclosure safeguards. The five controls shown here are Survey design, Weights, Precision, Model assumptions, Disclosure. Together, they prevent a health signal from being mistaken for an authorized decision.\n\n[Sources]\n- Canonical notebook V7_B_N12, SRAI Book 7 v1.0."}
